      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m concerned about a potential race condition with the swap slot. If the target process releases the memory, another process can claim that same swap slot before the writeback occurs. This would result in writing back data for the wrong process. The increased race window between zram_ioctl_process_writeback_scan and zram_writeback_slots makes this scenario more likely.\n\nTwo options \n\n1. Reduce the race window by introduce batch size limit: Instead of doing zram_ioctl_process_writeback_scan all at once and then let\u0027s have smaller steps\n\n2. Carry on the pte value the function and re-validate the PTE right before triggering the writeback. \n\n1 and 2 are orthogonal so we can have both, too.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 41
      },
